cad2bem does not include third-party source code, apart from the short excerpts of
Gmsh source in the patches of scripts/build_static_cad.ps1 (GPL-2.0-or-later, like
Gmsh). It uses the Gmsh C API: the
default build loads a separately installed Gmsh 4.15 library (GPL-2.0-or-later)
at run time, and the integrated build links Gmsh and OpenCASCADE Technology
(LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception) into the executable, with Gmsh's quadrilateral
recombination using the perfect matching of LEMON (Boost Software License 1.0)
instead of Blossom IV, which the integrated build leaves out. It is built from Rust
crates under permissive licences (MIT, Apache-2.0 and others). The executable
carries no font: the window uses the fonts of the operating system. See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
